From 7991bc04bba6db467460b375821a8ea30011786d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:13:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): refuse a no-pick chamfer on a partly bevelled edge
 loop by name

A 2D Chamfer with no picks classified each top loop whole, by the
farthest vertex from the wall. A loop with a modelled chamfer on one
side only read as bevelled (an extra vertex on the bevel's top edge)
or as sharp (no such vertex). The ride then cut the sharp sides, or
stood inside the part at the bevel. The verifier refused both as a
gouge at a coordinate, with no reason.

ride_loops now checks each matched top loop per segment (both ends
and the middle against the wall ring). A loop with a bevelled segment
and more than one width of sharp length refuses at generation. The
message names the bevelled part and the sharp part and asks for picks.
The check does not depend on tessellation.

All-sharp parts (#303), loops bevelled all round (#2435) and a sharp
loop beside a bevelled loop (#2596) are unchanged. The verifier is
unchanged.

Fixes #2887

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
